# {{ .Name }} (Resource)

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

## About

A BigQuery connection is how SELECT reads one GCP project's BigQuery usage and spend: the billing and pricing export it reads, and the service account it impersonates to reach the project. To learn more, see the [SELECT documentation](https://select.dev/docs/getting-started).

This resource is backed by SELECT's v2 API. The `api_key` configured on the provider must carry the `bigquery_connections:read` and `bigquery_connections:write` scopes; without them every operation fails with an authorization error.

